 Impact on Automobile business due to changes in the EV market environment 
 Given the changes in the EV (electric vehicle) market environment, during the year ended March 31, 2026, the Company revised its product launch plans and
reassessed its automobile electrification strategy and made decisions, including the cancellation of development and market launch of certain EV models. As a result, for the year ended March 31, 2026, the Company and its certain consolidated
subsidiaries recognized losses and expenses including impairment losses and losses on disposal of the related non-financial assets, impairment losses on investments accounted for using the equity method, and
provisions for EV-related losses. In the EV-related losses, as a result of the revision of the product launch plans described above, the Company and its certain
consolidated subsidiaries recognized losses and expenses of JPY 139,888 million in cost of sales, JPY 8,130 million in selling, general and administrative expenses, and JPY 89,245 million in research and development expenses in the
condensed consolidated statements of income for the six months ended September 30, 2025. 
 In connection with these
 EV-related losses, for the six months ended September 30, 2026, the Company and its certain consolidated subsidiaries recognized losses and expenses of JPY 479,244 million in cost of sales, and JPY
5,621 million in research and development expenses, and gains of JPY 49,722 million in share of profit (loss) of investments accounted for using the equity method in the condensed consolidated statements of income. These gains, losses and
expenses are included in Automobile business. The major components of these gains, losses and expenses are as follows. 
 Share of profit (loss) of
investments accounted for using the equity method 
 Share of profit (loss) of investments accounted for using the equity method includes a net gain of
JPY 41,789 million recognized by an affiliate of the Company, consisting of compensation from a certain consolidated subsidiary of the Company, partially offset by the associated EV-related losses. 
 Provisions for EV-related losses 
 Provisions for EV-related losses include provisions recognized due to changes in the EV market environment and the
reassessment of the automobile electrification strategy. Additional provisions recognized mainly include JPY 508,692 million losses or expenses arising from compensation to suppliers in connection with the procurement of parts of EV models,
based on discussions with the suppliers. 
 [B] Subsequent Event 
 Business combinations 
 The Company acquired an additional
21.0% of the common shares of Astemo, Ltd. (“Astemo”), an affiliate accounted for using the equity method. The acquisition was completed on October 1, 2026. The consideration for the acquisition of JPY 152,275 million was paid
in cash. Following the acquisition, the Company’s equity interest in Astemo increased from 40.0% to 61.0%, and Astemo became a subsidiary of the Company. 
 Astemo engages in the development, manufacture, sales and services of automotive components, transportation related components, industrial machines and
